Replying to my own post in an attempt to figure something out ...

I think pets know the strength of unarmed monsters but don't
make guesses as to the damage done by that monster's
weapons.

An unarmed kobald is a one bite fight to a pet small dog.  A
kobald armed with a wand of lightning is one mean SOB until
the wand runs out of zaps or your large dog is so strong that
lightning bolts don't phase him.

Often it seems that the watch captain is the first monster
with a very nice weapon that a pet encounters.  One swing
with that long sword or silver saber and more damage is done
than a watchman's wimpy dagger.  And so I seem to lose more
pets to the watch captain than to any other single cause.

Dwarves with mattocks have the same issue but they spend
so much time digging away from pets.  So do elves with elven
broadswords but elves seem to start appearing below mine town
in most of my games.



